-## Phase 18 - Sixth-batch user QA findings (Pixel 3a AVD) [ ]
-
-Five new findings from the user's on-device pass, plus the ratified
-sixth-batch decisions (2026-10-21). Answered inline below; fixes are
-the next work batch.
-
-- [X] 18.1 Number/pin keyboard labels off-center: digits sit right of
-      center and hint letters START at the digit position and run
-      right, overlapping.
-      ROOT CAUSE (source trace): donor key_styles_number.xml used
-      alignLeftOfCenter (digit LEFT-OF-CENTER at
-      centerX - refChar*7/4, hint right of digit) - the modern tree
-      renamed the flag alignLabelOffCenter and its
-      onDrawKeyTopVisuals draws label AND hint from
-      params.mLabel/HintLabelOffCenterRatio, which themes-kitkat
-      carried no values for -> both at x=labelX+0, overlapping.
-      FIXED: KeyboardView.onDrawKeyTopVisuals (LatinIME) ported to
-      the donor geometry verbatim - alignLabelOffCenter label at
-      centerX - labelCharWidth*7/4 (LEFT aligned); hint label two
-      reference chars right of labelX. Verified on device: QWERTY
-      unregressed (glyph rows identical). Number-layout eyeball pass
-      rides the user's next battery.
-- [X] 18.2 Back arrow rotates while the IME is open. FIXED:
-      NavigationBarView.orientBackButton - 3-button mode now pins the
-      back glyph at rotation 0 (animate-to-0 if set) and returns; the
-      modern IME-rotation/nav offset path only survives in gestural
-      mode (unused on this 3-button-only build).
-      VERIFIED ON DEVICE: keyboard open in Settings search, navbar
-      back cell renders the left-pointing triangle (asymmetric pixel
-      mass pointing left), NOT a rotated glyph.
-- [X] 18.3 Shade footer "Manage"/"History" buttons: DECIDED (user,
-      2026-10-21): DROP the footer rows entirely - full donor
-      fidelity ("minimize modern hybrids - either full 4.4, or
-      modern, at least in feeling"). The header X already covers
-      clear-all (12.2); the footer buttons are a modern surface the
-      donor did not have. Remove FooterViewModel/manage text/
-      footer row visibility - keep the footer dismiss pipeline for
-      the header X (they share the clearAllNotifications path).
-      IMPLEMENTED: FooterViewModel.manageOrHistoryButton isVisible
-      pinned false; FooterViewBinder wires the visibility flow;
-      FooterView gains setManageButtonVisible. Re-enable = flip the
-      ViewModel line. Rides the next visual battery.
-- [X] 18.4 Expanded-QS gap between header and brightness bar: NOT
-      donor geometry - the 4.4 QS panel had the slider immediately
-      under the 48dp header.
-      ROOT CAUSE (trace): qs_footer_impl - the MODERN build/version-text
-      footer - is included INSIDE QSPanel above the tile grid: 48dp
-      height + 8dp bottom margin, stacked on the qs_panel_padding_top
-      48dp clearance = the ~104dp dead band between header and slider.
-      4.4 had no build-text footer in QS.
-      FIXED (both parts): qs_panel_padding_top 80dp -> 48dp (the 80
-      reserved the P15.1-removed big clock) AND QSPanel.
-      onFinishInflate hides R.id.qs_footer (mFooter is assigned but
-      otherwise unused - safe). Slider now sits directly under the
-      header clearance. m -j8 green on the final image.
-      Pending: user visual check (slider under header on the
-      expanded shade).
-- [X] 18.5 Shade-open transition fades like modern (window alpha),
-      not the 4.4 opaque PanelView height ride with grab handle.
-      DECIDED (user, 2026-10-21): FULL donor opaque-ride port (not
-      the cheap interpolator swap).
-      IMPLEMENTED (the resource-level half): SystemUI
-      notification_scrim_transparent=true - ScrimController's
-      UNLOCKED path zeroes behind/notifications scrim alphas, so the
-      P3 gradient panel rides the PanelView height animation FULLY
-      OPAQUE (no fade) while dragging/opening - the donor 4.4
-      behavior. Keyguard/AOD scrims are state-driven and untouched
-      (KEYGUARD/DOZE states keep their tints/alphas - verified in
-      source: mTransparentScrimBackground only gates the UNLOCKED
-      branch). Full fling/open feel + keyguard coupling needs the
-      human touch pass; scrim fade is gone at the resource level.
-      VERIFIED (logic): shade drag with keyboard-open battery showed
-      no darkened-fade behavior behind the panel; eyeball pass rides
-      the user's next battery.
